          "heading": "Jack van Poortvliet signs multi-year Leicester deal, eyeing England's 2027 World Cup",
          "body": "England scrum-half Jack van Poortvliet has signed a new multi-year deal with Leicester Tigers. The 25-year-old has made 118 first-team appearances since graduating in 2019, and he already holds an England contract for 2026-27. Van Poortvliet, who has 27 England caps, missed the 2023 World Cup after an ankle injury in a warm-up game, and he will hope to play a big role in England's 2027 World Cup campaign in Australia. \"It was a pretty easy decision to stay,\" he told the club website."
